  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n Spiritual\n Translation\n\n\n##\n ¶5\n\nThe Divine\n Wisdom proceeding —\n the great\n Intellectual\n of\n heaven\n — together\n with the first\n state of the\n regener\nating will in\n its initial vigor,\n gov\nerns through\n the complete\n ordering of spiritual truths:\n the full\n body of revealed doctrine in all\n its distinct forms,\n and\n every\n derivative\n understanding\n that proceeds\n from it. The seven\n holy\n foundational principles upon which all interior perception\n rests stand\n imm\nov\nable\n.\n The vast\n expanse of natural cognitions encompasses\n the whole external mind. The four cardinal\n tru\nths of\n order\n extend\n to every quarter of the mind, up\nholding the power of divine arrangement in\n the natural degree,\n which is the ultimate plane\n upon which all heavenly states rest as\n upon\n their\n foundation\n. The five essential faculties proceeding\n from the Divine Human are those by which\n the whole mind is established in stable form\n. The calling\n-\nforth of divine truth and the answering\n reception of\n the will —\n together\n with in\ndestructible wisdom, truth so\n confirmed it cannot be shattered — these\n become advers\naries to\n all\n that\n opp\noses them, and\n yet\n it\n is\n they who govern all things.\n\n##\n ¶6\n\nIn\n the lower\n degree\n of the mind, the complete\n truths of faith and charity stand\n firm in\n their fullness.\n The forms\n in\n which these truths present themselves to perception\n are according\n to their\n number\n. The three essential\n sustaining principles — love, wisdom,\n and use — uphold the sphere of\n spiritual illumination. The remaining\n three are\n the external\n truths with which the Divine Life clothes\n the regenerating mind; they were best\nowed in the state of reformation and projected\n outward together\n with what\n is contained\n within them,\n made manifest in\n the forms of the mind. What stands\n perf\nected before the guardian\n principle at the threshold between interior and exterior\n states —\n the one who gov\nerns passage between degrees by his\n own sovereign\n power — these\n are\n the three essential divine\n principles that operate\n in\n the midst of human minds. Whoever\n comes to perce\nive them and commits their very life into\n the\n keeping\n of these governing truths is thereby sustained\n.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "The [Wisdom] and the great [Light of the heavens] and the great Mind that is [over all, and] this Youth that is with the [First Man; the] thirty-six angels [and the] twenty-two angels [that are beneath them;] but [the number] of the twenty-two [proceeds from the thirty-six;] the seven pillars that stan[d immovable;] the sea that surrounds the universe [on every side; the] four angels that are distributed to the [four corners of the] universe, supporting the mightiness [that is] below, which is the earth of all the heavens [and their foundation;] these other five gods, the sons of the Man, they that [sustain all, by whom] the universe is stood firm [in its order;] the Summons and the Obedience [, together with] the splendour of the [Light] and the Adamant of Light [;] they are become enemies [to all that opposes them, yet] they guide it."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "The third also, [\nwhich is] below, there are twelve\n powers standing firm there. However, the\n number of the twelve images [proceeds from\n them;] the three great pillars\n of mightiness that [are the\n] pillars supporting the disk [of\n light;] the other three [also\n,] they are the garments that\n the Living Spirit [fashioned;]\n he put them at that time [upon\n the powers] that threw them, together\n with [the light] which is displayed\n therein [;] this [that\n stands] perfect before [the] great\n Porter [who abides] in his\n power [;] these are the three\n great [powers that contend] against\n [all evil. They] are in\n the midst of people [; whoever]\n knows [them and] entrusts\n his soul to them [is preserved]."
    }
  ],
